extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 26: Dinosaur Swamp printed 66-69 (cache p067-p070, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the OCR and checked against 150 dpi renders of printed 68 (right column) and 69 (left column); the OCR of the mutation tables on 67-68 agrees with the render''s figures where checked. The entry starts at the Mutant Barbarian R.C.C. heading on printed 66 and ends with the tribe-size note on printed 69, above O.C.C.s from Rifts & Sourcebooks. || KIND: an R.C.C., a mutant human race, so men_of_arms is false as for every race. The entry prints its own skills, so it is a complete class: R.C.C. Skills, R.C.C. Related Skills (two each from Domestic, Physical or W.P., and Wilderness, stored as count 6 with three floors of two, plus one at 4, 8, 12 and 15) and two Secondary Skills are stored as printed. The row brief expected zero related and secondary skills, the rule for a race whose skills come from an occupation; this page prints them (2026-10-20). || XP: the first column of the Experience Point Tables, printed 74 (cache p075), shared with the Legacy Scout; read off a 300 dpi render by the row 3a worker and identical to the Legacy Scout''s stored ladder. Stored because the book prints a ladder for this class. || POOLS: hit points are not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s O.C.C.s. S.D.C. is a bonus of 3D6+16 to physical S.D.C., stored as bonuses.pools.sdc. P.P.E. 4D6+6, no growth. || BONUSES: +2 to roll with impact (combat.roll); +1D4 P.E. or +1D6+1 Spd is a choice group. The Alert and Ready bonuses apply only in the wilderness and are prose. || PSIONICS (2026-10-20): two tables on printed 68, stored as two banded choose-1 groups with psionics_allowed false, the shape BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F118 gives a race with its own psionics table. Table A (01-40 Minor, 41-90 none, 91-00 Master) records the roll and carries no block. Table B (the number of powers and when they manifest) carries a full minor psionics block on each row: I.S.P. 4D6+6 +1D6 per level, powers from the nine named on printed 68 (Bio-Regenerate (Self) is the catalog Bio-Regenerate (self), and Impervious to Poison is the catalog Impervious to Poison/Toxin), with later manifestations as powers_schedule entries. An unbanded Not Psychic option on table B is for a character who is not a Minor Psychic. The Master Psychic row points at the Barbarian Psychic, one of the four barbarian versions left by Nate''s D18 (2026-10-19). || MUTATIONS (2026-10-20): the Number of Mutations table (printed 67) is a banded choose-1 group that records the count. The Mutant Features table (printed 67-68, 32 rows covering 01-00) is prose in the 1. Random Mutations ability, not a pick group: the book rolls on it zero to three times by the first table, and a rolls group must be held to a fixed count or to dice, neither of which the book gives. Its bonuses are not applied. The extra psychic power on the 61-80 and 91-00 count rows is prose. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Lore: Dinosaur is this book''s special skill Lore: Dinosaurs; Imitate Voices (and Animal Sounds) is Imitate Voices & Sounds; Identify Plants & Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit; Athletics (General) is Athletics (general); Speak Native Language at 88% is Language: Native Tongue. W.P. Archery & Targeting or one Ancient W.P., one Ancient W.P. and one Modern W.P. are three choice groups; the catalog does not separate Ancient from Modern. Interrogation Technique is the Espionage row Interrogation; Kayaking/Canoes is Boat: Paddle Types/Canoe/Kayak; Hovercycle is Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes. Technical excludes the two Technical computer rows and Photography; other tech-based skills is in the note. Hand to Hand Expert; Assassin for an Anarchist or evil alignment costs one related skill. || EQUIPMENT: clothes, boots or moccasins, utility belt, small backpack or satchel, canteen, a metal knife, a stone skinning knife, 100 feet of fishing line with hooks, 1D4 animal snares. Not stored: 2D6 miscellaneous pocket items, armor (typically homespun or an Eco-Wizard creation; Huntsman armor, 40 M.D.C., is popular, and Homespun suits for Mutants carry 1D6+10 more M.D.C. to the main body), and weapons (anything from M.D. weapons to handmade, SteelTree and Eco-Wizard weapons). || NOT STORED: female Mutant Barbarians share the human Nurturer''s skills and background (a barbarian version left by D18); tribe sizes and enemies are in the GM notes."
