# Mutant Barbarian

## Lore

Mutant Barbarians are the tribes of Dinosaur Swamp in whom random mutation runs strongest: part Wilderness Scout, part Vagabond warrior and part instinctive animal. Generations in the wild have made them resistant to disease and poison and given them keen senses, and many carry a few psychic powers or strange physical features. A mutation may mark a whole tribe, a generation or a single child, and some tribes can no longer breed outside a narrow line. Their mutations are both their advantage and the deformity that sets them apart.

They lean on their natural abilities and make stone-age tools and weapons of wood, bone, stone, sinew and hide, well balanced enough to match modern ones, adapting a Vibro-Knife or M.D.C. scrap where they can. They raid like predators rather than bandits, taking food, livestock, clothing, weapons and tools and ignoring machines and valuables. A stare or a refusal to back down is a challenge, and a lot of spilled blood can drive them into a frenzy. They avoid the big predators and prey on small dinosaurs, mammals and other humanoids.

## GM Notes

The Mutant Features table is in the 1. Random Mutations ability: roll the Number of Mutations group first, then roll on the table that many times and record each result and its bonuses by hand.

Mutant Barbarians regard the Splugorth, Horune Pirates and D-Bees foreign to the region as invaders and mortal enemies, Slavers and Horune above all. Outsiders, other barbarian tribes, Native Americans, Psi-Stalkers and settlers are rivals to be robbed, and Mutants are more likely than human barbarians to kill when resisted.

Armor is light: a homespun non-environmental suit (see the Wild Knives Warrior; a Mutant''s suit can carry 1D6+10 more M.D.C. to the main body) or an Eco-Wizard creation, and Huntsman armor (40 M.D.C.) is popular. Weapons range from M.D. weapons to handmade S.D.C. ones, SteelTree, and Eco-Wizard, Techno-Wizard, rune and Bio-Wizard items, which they love. Starting kit beyond the sheet: 2D6 miscellaneous pocket items.

Female Mutant Barbarians have the same skills and background as the human barbarian Nurturer. Tribes number 40 to 240, seldom more than 1,000, and Mutants are about 15% of the barbarian population.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-barbarian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-barbarian';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-mutant-barbarian-class.sql');
